{"word": "quantitative", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "quantitative", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "adjective", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkwɒntɪtətɪv/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkwɒntətɪv/", "tags": ["UK"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkwɑn.təˌteɪ.tɪv/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈkwɑn.təˌteɪ.ɾɪv]", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkwɑn.əˌteɪ.tɪv/", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈkwɑn.əˌteɪ.ɾɪv]", "tags": ["General American"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈkwɑn.tɪˌteɪ.tɪv/", "tags": ["US"]}], "forms": [{"word": "more quantitative", "tags": ["comparative"]}, {"word": "most quantitative", "tags": ["superlative"]}, {"word": "quantitive", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Of a measurements and data types: based on some quantity or number rather than on some quality.", "tags": [], "examples": ["Near-synonyms: nonqualitative, unqualitative", "quantitative data", "A yes-no data field is qualitative, whereas a number-value data field is quantitative."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["nonqualitative", "unqualitative"], "antonyms": ["nonquantitative", "unquantitative"], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Of logical analysis: based on quantification as well as qualification, rather than solely the latter: thus, not ignorant of magnitudes (large or small).", "tags": [], "examples": ["quantitative analysis", "It's easy to say, qualitatively, that an undesirable thing should be banned and punishable; but the law must often also be quantitative if it is to be fair, which may sometimes mean that some small number of parts per trillion is an acceptable amount."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["nonquantitative", "unquantitative"], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(chemistry) Of a form of analysis, that determines the amount of some element or compound in a sample.", "tags": [], "examples": ["quantitative analysis", "The lab tests that are currently commercially available for this pollutant can tell us a yes-no answer as to whether it was detected, but they cannot provide a quantitative result; a new generation of quantitative assays is under development."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": ["nonquantitative", "unquantitative"], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "коли́чествен"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "定量的"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "kvantitatiivinen"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "määrällinen"}, {"language": {"code": "id", "name": "Indonesian"}, "word": "kuantitatif"}, {"language": {"code": "lt", "name": "Lithuanian"}, "word": "kiekybinis"}, {"language": {"code": "ms", "name": "Malay"}, "word": "kuantitatif"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "quantitativo"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "cantitativ"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "коли́чественный"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "kvantitativ"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "kvantitativt"}, {"language": {"code": "vi", "name": "Vietnamese"}, "word": "định lượng"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quantitative", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}